      "message": "Why not represent this as a\n```\nstruct BootArg\u003c\u0027a\u003e {\n    arg: \u0026\u0027a [u8],\n    equal_sign: Option\u003cusize\u003e,\n}\n\nimpl AsRef\u003c[u8]\u003e for Bootarg {\n    fn as_ref(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[u8] { return self.arg }\n}\n\nimpl Bootarg {\n    pub fn name(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[u8] {\n        if let Some(n) \u003d self.equal_sign {\n            self.arg[..n]\n        } else {\n            self.arg\n        };\n    }\n\n    pub fn value(\u0026self) -\u003e Option\u003c\u0026[u8]\u003e {\n        Some(self.arg[self.equal_sign?..])\n    }\n}\n```\nthen\n```\nnew_bootargs.extend_from_slice(arg.as_ref())\n```\n?",
